# ── Terraform ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# State, plans and provider plugins are never committed. A committed state file
# is a committed database dump, including every value Terraform saw — and the plan
# JSON is a full description of every resource about to be created.
.terraform/
.terraform.tfstate.lock.info
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
tfplan
crash.log
crash.*.log
# Local variable files may carry values that are not in the repo. The committed
# *.tfvars files hold no secrets by construction; a `*.auto.tfvars` is by
# definition local.
*.auto.tfvars
*.auto.tfvars.json
# Override files are the classic way a secret enters a Terraform tree.
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json
